WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:05.291
Most decks have too many pictures, too small, placed wherever there was room.

2
00:00:05.341 --> 00:00:07.173
The fix isn't design talent.

3
00:00:07.223 --> 00:00:09.021
It's a few simple rules.

4
00:00:10.021 --> 00:00:15.116
Before you add any image, ask one question: what would the viewer lose without it?

5
00:00:15.166 --> 00:00:17.822
If the answer is nothing, leave it out.

6
00:00:18.822 --> 00:00:22.117
One strong image at full width beats three small ones.

7
00:00:22.167 --> 00:00:25.010
Then crop away anything that doesn't support the point.

8
00:00:26.510 --> 00:00:28.481
Pick one layout per slide.

9
00:00:28.531 --> 00:00:33.905
If a headline sits over a photo, find the quiet part, or add a contrast band behind it.

10
00:00:35.405 --> 00:00:39.211
Four tiny product photos became one large shot of the Trail Pack.

11
00:00:39.261 --> 00:00:42.614
One image, one claim, one sentence of support.

12
00:00:42.664 --> 00:00:44.694
The narration does the rest.

13
00:00:45.805 --> 00:00:48.636
Fewer, bigger images make a better video.

14
00:00:48.686 --> 00:00:53.536
On Pro, AI directs it, framing each picture as a scene timed to your voice.

15
00:00:53.586 --> 00:00:56.638
Try Basic first at powerpoint2vid.com.

